course: dictionary
lesson: 6964
title: One word, many meanings: pan
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: The word pan has more than one meaning. Read the words around it to find out which one the writer means. «Walk, never run, in the kitchen: knives, hot pans and slippery floors make running dangerous.» The kitchen and the knives tell you that a pan is a cooking pot.
explain: Pan can also be an action word. «To pan for gold» means washing river sand in a pan to find gold. Gold rush miners did this in California, Australia and New Zealand. The word «for» and the idea of searching are your clues.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «A family in Ohio left a pan of oil on the hob» still makes sense with pan meaning a cooking pot. If you tried the meaning of a balance scale dish instead, it would not fit. The context decides which meaning is right.
fact: A pan is a metal pot for cooking food, often with a long handle.
fact: A pan is also one of the two dishes of a balance scale.
fact: A baking pan or tin holds cakes in the oven.
fact: Pan can be a verb too: to pan for gold is to wash river sand in a pan to find gold.
fact: To pan a film means to say it is very bad.
exercise: «Walk, never run, in the kitchen: knives, hot pans and slippery floors make running dangerous.» In this sentence, what is a pan? | A pot for cooking food | *A metal cooking pot | A dish of a balance scale | To wash river sand
exercise: «The heavier pan of the scale sank down.» Which meaning of pan is this? | To say a film is bad | A baking tin for cakes | To wash river sand for gold | *One of the two dishes of a balance scale
exercise: Gold rush miners did this to find gold: they washed river sand. What does «to pan for gold» mean? | Cooked eggs in a frying pan | Said a film was bad | Baked cakes in a tin | *Washed river sand in a pan to find gold
test: «Bake the sponge in a round pan for twenty minutes.» What is a pan in this sentence? | *A baking pan or tin for the oven | A cooking pot for the hob | To wash river sand | A dish of a balance scale
test: Ella says, «The critics panned the film.» What does she mean? | The film was washed in a river | The film was cooked in a pan | *The critics said the film was very bad | The film was very funny and happy
exam: «Searing meat cooks its outside fast on a very hot pan until brown.» What does pan mean in this sentence? | A baking tin for cakes | A dish of a balance scale | To pan for gold | *A metal cooking pot
